Falsifies `byte_glob::verification::the_dot_rule_only_touches_names_that_start_with_a_dot`.

The defect: the leading-dot rule loses its test on the name, so under `LeadingDot::Special` every name is refused
unless the pattern opens with a literal dot, not only the dotfiles.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(special, ordinary)` for a name that does not start with `.`.

diff --git a/crates/byte_glob/src/lib.rs b/crates/byte_glob/src/lib.rs
index 1d603e71b..05c20fcd5 100644
--- a/crates/byte_glob/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/byte_glob/src/lib.rs
@@ -164,3 +164,2 @@ pub fn match_steps(pattern: &[u8], name: &[u8], dot: LeadingDot) -> (bool, usize
     if dot == LeadingDot::Special
-        && name.first() == Some(&b'.')
         && !opens_with_a_literal_dot(pattern)
